From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] shell: separate backdrop blur from reduce transparency

Backdrop blur samples the framebuffer behind each blurred surface on
every repaint. On devices where that is costly, the backdrop-blur
shell-state key turns the blur off while surfaces keep their
translucent fill. reduce-transparency still makes surfaces opaque.

